# An Interactive Journey Through Functional Fibres

A functional observation keeps a behavioral label while potentially forgetting other coordinates. Begin with the [mathematical idea of a fibre](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fiber_(mathematics)): all total states mapped to one observable profile.

{{interactive_demo:0}}

The first widget exposes the split model directly. The behavioral label stays fixed while awareness toggles. This reversible switch is the canonical twin construction.

{{visualization:0}}

{{algorithm:0}}

<details><summary>Reveal the unique-twin argument</summary>
For an aware state $(b,1)$, functional identity forces any twin to have first coordinate $b$, and voidness forces second coordinate $0$. Therefore $(b,0)$ exists and is unique.
</details>

## Can experience be reconstructed?

The exact criterion is fibre constancy: a rule depending only on behavior can recover experience precisely when no functional fibre contains conflicting experience values. Explore finite data below.

